Coursera, edX, and Khan Academy together have over 200 million registered users globally — an order of magnitude more than all traditional universities combined, reaching populations otherwise excluded.
Learners in low-income countries who complete online courses from US/UK universities earn salary premiums of 20–50% compared to local degree holders, according to Coursera economic impact data.
The cost of delivering online education is 60–80% lower per student than residential university education, making quality learning accessible to populations excluded by tuition cost.
